Let's start with the observation that what is currently presented as Artificial
Intelligence is indeed as artificial as can be. It doesn't come spontaneously out
of silicon fed with lots of energy. It's essentially the results of human
intelligence collected and presented in a specific way. The cornerstone of this
technology is Large Language Models (\LLM{}s), where language is interpreted rather
liberally, because images are also part of the game and the languages meant for
computers are also fed into the machinery.

